# Placeholders only. No secret belongs in this file. Nothing loads it
# automatically: the Go server reads the real process environment, so export
# the variables or prefix the command with `env`. See docs/development/getting-started.md.

# Go server (services/core). Defaults are shown. Every value is validated at
# start-up and a wrong or unknown MORNINGSTAR_* variable stops the server.
#
# The listen address must be a loopback IP literal. Wildcard, LAN and
# hostname values are refused.
# MORNINGSTAR_HTTP_LISTEN=127.0.0.1:8080
#
# Exact Host header allow-list, comma separated. Loopback names only.
# Default: the listen address and localhost on the same port.
# MORNINGSTAR_HTTP_ALLOWED_HOSTS=127.0.0.1:8080,localhost:8080
#
# debug, info, warn or error
# MORNINGSTAR_LOG_LEVEL=info
# json or text
# MORNINGSTAR_LOG_FORMAT=json

# Web UI (apps/web). Origin of the Go API for the same-origin rewrite.
# Read by next.config.ts when `next build` or `next dev` starts. Changing it
# needs a new build. Loopback hosts only. May be set in apps/web/.env.local,
# which Git ignores. The Go server accepts this name and ignores its value, so
# it can sit in the same shared environment.
# MORNINGSTAR_API_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:8080
